Angela Merkel is the Chancellor of  Germany Europe's largest economy she is  an unglamorous leader and often  underrated that has a sharp analytical  mind she's not one to back down from a  good fight and can be surprisingly  decisive this is a brief history of  Angela Merkel 1954 Hamburg has been  devastated by world war ii anglich  Asner's born germany is in the midst of  the Cold War standoff between the  Soviets in the West against the wave of  migrants Angela's pastor father moves  the family to a small farming village in  the communist piece 1957 the Kassner  family moves again to Temple in East  Germany a market town of 20,000 Angela's  father sets up a Theological Seminary  1961 the Berlin wall goes up kazna  remembers her mother crying in church  1973 Kassner graduates from high school  she moves to Leipzig to attend  University she studies physics the only  subject she'd failed in high school  1977 Kasner marries fellow physics  student Ulrich Merkel and takes his name  they moved to Berlin 1982 Angela  divorces Ulrich she keeps his name 1986  Merkel completes her PhD in quantum  chemistry she meets Joaquim Sauer her  second husband 1989 the Berlin Wall  Falls and so does East Germany's  communist regime Merkel is working out  of physics labs she joins a crowd  pushing past guards into West Berlin she  becomes involved in East Germany's  pro-democracy movement  1990 Lothar de Maiziere becomes East  Germany's last Prime Minister he chooses  Merkel to be his deputy press secretary  she ends up joining the West German  political party the Christian Democratic  Union in the first election of a  reunited Germany she wins a seat in  parliament 1991 Merkel is appointed  Federal Minister for women and youth  under Chancellor Helmut Kohl wanted an  Easterner and a woman on his cab in 1994  Merkel is promoted to minister for the  environment and nuclear safety 1998 :  ministration is defeated in election and  rocked by scandal Merkel surprises her  own party and swoops in to become its  secretary-general and later the  chairperson 2005 in a special election  Merkel narrowly defeats Gerhard  schröder's Social Democratic Party  becoming Germany's first female  Chancellor 2008 the financial crisis  takes hold in the US and Europe Merkel  bails out Germany's banks she also  commits to fiscal austerity to deal with  growing debt 2009 Merkel wins a second  term 2010 Germany's economy recovers  faster than that of any other country in  Europe Merkel helps craft a bailout for  Greece holding the eurozone together  2013 thanks largely to a stable German  labor market Merkel wins a third term in  a landslide victory 2014 crisis breaks  out in Ukraine Merkel is forced to  confront Vladimir Putin over Russia's  actions 2015 against the wishes of her  party Merkel accepts growing numbers of  refugees from the Middle East she urges  the rest of the EU to follow suit Merkel  has kept her style of leadership modest  and plain-spoken  but she has edged Germany into a more  assertive role during the 10 years as  Chancellor  you
 

